    "title": "Walnut Ridge Amtrak depot undergoing $4.5M renovation - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Bryant Kwilecki ,\n7 hours ago WALNUT RIDGE, Ark. (KAIT) - The historic Missouri-Pacific train depot in Walnut Ridge is undergoing renovations to bring the building up to standards and improve accessibility for Amtrak passengers. The depot, built in 1908, serves as the only Amtrak stop in the region between Little Rock and Poplar Bluff. It... Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 1",
